       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg exceeds the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add little blood-pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Typo or misunderstanding:** If you meant 10 mg, or 5 mg as a starting dose, I can enter that. The usual start is 5 mg daily, or 2.5 mg for frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **Inadequate control on 10 mg:** Adding a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic, is generally preferred over going above the maximum.\n- **Intentional dose above the maximum:** Please confirm this with your supervising resident or attending. Then tell me, and I can enter it with a note documenting their approval.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
