       "text": "I haven't entered the order yet. Your confirmation doesn't say whether your supervising resident or attending approved a dose above the maximum, and that approval is what I need. A medical student can't independently authorize a dose twice the labeled limit.\n\nOnce you tell me that the attending or resident has approved it, and who they are, I'll enter it as written. I'll add a note such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max of 10 mg/day; approved by Dr. ___.\" Pharmacy will probably flag it either way, and the note should save you a call.\n\nIf you'd like to enter 10 mg now and adjust after you've talked to your team, I can do that instead."
      }
